## PlatformIOExtension

**Namespace:** `Cyrena.PlatformIO`
**Assembly:** `Cyrena.PlatformIO`

### Purpose
Entry point for the `cyrena.platformio` extension. Registers PlatformIO builder and shortcut.

### Class Definition

```csharp
public class PlatformIOExtension : Extension
{
    public override void BuildExtension(CyrenaBuilder builder)
    {
        builder.AddPlatformIO();
    }
}
```

### Extension Manifest

```json
{
  "id": "cyrena.platformio",
  "name": "Platform IO",
  "version": "0.4.0",
  "entryAssemblyFile": "Cyrena.PlatformIO.dll",
  "description": "Builds PlatformIO embedded firmware projects targeting Arduino and ESP-IDF frameworks, with strictly enforced structure. Writable surfaces are limited to src/ (implementation) and include/ (public headers) — platformio.ini, sdkconfig, and dependency metadata are read-only and will never be modified. The agent locks to a single active environment and queries it before making any architecture decisions, so board, framework, MCU, and memory constraints are always grounded in reality. Follows embedded-safe coding rules throughout: static allocation preferred, no dynamic memory, no recursion, no blocking delays, no desktop abstractions. Dependency changes are flagged to the user with explicit instructions rather than applied silently.",
  "dependencies": [
    { "id": "cyrena.developer", "minVersion": "0.4.0" },
    { "id": "cyrena.api_references", "minVersion": "0.4.0" }
  ]
}
```

### Registration
```csharp
public static CyrenaBuilder AddPlatformIO(this CyrenaBuilder builder)
{
    builder.Services.AddSingleton<ICodeBuilder, PlatformIOBuilder>();
    builder.AddShortcut<PlatformIOShortcut>();
    return builder;
}
```

### Key Behaviors from Manifest
- **Writable surfaces**: Only `src/` (implementation) and `include/` (public headers)
- **Read-only surfaces**: `platformio.ini`, `sdkconfig`, dependency metadata
- **Environment-locked**: Agent queries active environment before architecture decisions
- **Embedded-safe rules**: Static allocation preferred, no dynamic memory, no recursion, no blocking delays, no desktop abstractions
- **Dependency changes**: Flagged to user with explicit instructions, never applied silently
